  "context": "Guardrails: work only in linked worktrees; never git add -A; Joe Harris identity, no agent trailers; no explanatory code/YAML comments (make comment-policy-check); no new CI skips, no required-check renames, no ruleset/settings/secret changes; no weakening of an existing check beyond the rule this item names; durable commit text without tracker ids. Do not change credentials, the broker, gateway clients or secrets. Host reinstall happens only after merge, from origin/develop.",
  "description": "_project/scripts/review_gateway_host.sh check_usage_probes marks the whole gateway degraded when \"omp auth-gateway check\" fails for any broker login. Today it fails only for antigravity-cli (OAuth refresh 500), which the gateway does not serve; anthropic, openai-codex and google-antigravity are ok. cmd_monitor publishes on every state change, so brief failures opened and closed four issues (#4231, #4232, #4271, #4275) in two days.\n\nChange: read the probe output per provider; a failure for a provider the gateway serves stays degraded, a failure for any other provider becomes a notice naming it. In cmd_monitor, publish (notify and issue) only when the same new signature is seen on two consecutive runs; keep a pending signature in the state directory. Keep the rule that an unfiled issue leaves the state unrecorded.\n\nScope: _project/scripts/review_gateway_host.sh, tests/unit/scripts/test_review_gateway_host.py, docs/internal/review-gateway-host.md.",
